			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@benschwarz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>benschwarz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@eleventy\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eleventy</span></a></span> Did I mention that I once wrote a JS library that used inline XML (DocBook) and custom XSLT-FO templates to generate documentation?</p><p>Or that I once wrote custom OpenLDAP schemas to build a web Auth system?</p><p>Or that I once used XSLT in Oracle 8i Java Stored Proceedures to do templating?</p><p>If you don't have regrets, you aren't trying hard enough.</p>",
